      "narrative": "The morning light through the shuttered windows of the Copper Finch cuts a pale stripe across the scarred tabletop. You turn to Mara Venn, who sits nursing a cup of cold tea, her charcoal coat pulled tight against the damp.\n\nYou ask about the Ash Gate.\n\nMara's eyes flick to you, sharp and appraising. She sets her cup down with a soft clack.\n\n\"The Ash Gate?\"\n\nShe leans back, studying you like a merchant weighing a coin. Her fingers drum once on the table.\n\n\"I could tell you,\" she says slowly. \"But first \u2014 what's a ranger doing asking about a sealed gate at this hour, without so much as a blade drawn or a story offered in trade?\"\n\nToran Vex, the ink-stained clerk at the next table, glances up from a sheaf of papers. His shoulders hitch \u2014 a nervous tic \u2014 and he looks back down quickly, pretending he wasn't listening.\n\nMara's gaze doesn't waver. She's waiting."
    },
