      "narrative": "Mara Venn's smile tightens. She holds your gaze for a long moment, then her attention drifts \u2014 deliberately \u2014 to a crack in the wall, a stain on the ceiling, anywhere but you.\n\n\"You press hard, don't you?\" she says, her voice cooling. \"I told you what I know. Bram kept the gate. Bram's dead. The lock's filed. That's the shape of it.\"\n\nShe picks up her tea again, but doesn't drink. Just holds it, a barrier between you.\n\nToran Vex shifts in his seat, his quill scratching a nervous line across his paper. He doesn't look up.\n\nThe question hangs unanswered. Mara's given you nothing new \u2014 no name, no thread, no crack to pry open. The silence in the Copper Finch stretches thin, and the morning light through the shutters does nothing to warm it."
    },
