      "narrative": "Your voice cuts the stillness \u2014 \"Old Bram!\" \u2014 the name echoing off the cracked stone, swallowed by the grey morning. The sound travels, thins, and dies against the rusted iron of the gate.\n\nNothing answers. No shuffle of feet. No creak of old joints. No voice from beyond.\n\nThe crow shifts on the arch, ruffling its feathers. It lets out a single sharp *caw*, then settles back into silence, watching you with a black, unblinking eye.\n\nThe gate stands sealed. The stain at the base of the arch is dark and old. The filed lock hangs motionless.\n\nThe only sound is the wind, threading through the gap between the gate and the stone \u2014 a thin, high whisper, like air forced through a cracked tooth.\n\nOld Bram is dead. The world has already told you this. The silence where his name fell is its own answer."
