      "narrative": "You drop to a knee at the base of the arch, fingers brushing the cold stone. The dark stain spreads beneath your hand \u2014 old, crusted, indistinguishable from years of weather and grime. You can't tell if it's blood, oil, or just the slow sweat of damp rock. It offers nothing.\n\nYou trace the scratches on the stone beside the hasp. Your nail catches in a few shallow grooves, but they follow the grain of the rock \u2014 natural erosion, water and wind over decades, not a blade or a claw. Nothing deliberate. Nothing that tells a story.\n\nThe crow cocks its head, watching your failure with the patience of something that has no stake in your questions.\n\nThe ground beneath the arch holds its secrets. You found nothing useful here."
