      "narrative": "The Copper Finch's door groans open, and the warmth of the common room wraps around you again \u2014 woodsmoke, old ale, the faint salt of dried meat. A few heads turn at your entrance, then look away. Morning drinkers keep to themselves.\n\nYour table stands where you left it: scarred oak near the back wall, the surface crosshatched with the marks of old knives and spilled cups. A tallow candle gutters in a clay dish, its flame thin and wavering.\n\nThe room is quiet. A woman in a patched cloak nurses something dark at the bar. The barkeep wipes a cup with a rag that may once have been white. Neither looks your way.\n\nMara Venn is not here. Her chair by the hearth is empty. The embers in the grate have settled to ash.\n\nToran Vex remains at his corner table, head bent over a fresh sheet of paper, his quill moving in short, nervous strokes. He hasn't looked up since you entered."
